# Declare an API and participant

`contract.trellis` is the source of truth for both the public API and the participant that implements it.

```trellis
api "acme.orders@v1" {
  version "1.0.0";
  display_name "Orders";
  description "Order management API.";

  model CreateOrderRequest {
    customerId: string;
  }

  model CreateOrderResponse {
    orderId: string;
  }

  rpc "Orders.Create" {
    version "v1";
    input CreateOrderRequest;
    output CreateOrderResponse;
  }
}

participant "acme.orders-service@v1" service {
  implements "acme.orders@v1";
}
```

Run `trellis generate`. The canonical `trellis.api.v1` and `trellis.participant.v1` artifacts are emitted before language SDKs are replaced.

The API declares the public vocabulary. The participant declares who implements
it and which other APIs and resources it needs. Keep these identities distinct:
more than one participant can implement an API, and an API release version is
not a transport version.

Add TypeScript output configuration to `trellis.toml` as shown in
[setup](/guides/write-a-service/setup). Import the generated participant from
`.trellis/ts/participants/acme-orders-service/mod.ts`. SDK types and descriptors
come from `.trellis/ts/apis/`; do not duplicate models in service code.

Generation validates the entire project before replacing the last successful
outputs. Fix errors in IDL and regenerate rather than editing generated files.
Check in authored source and `trellis.lock`; keep `.trellis/` disposable.
